    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49491" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">turpĭcŭlus</span></b> , a,
		um, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>adj.
				dim.</i> [turpis], <i>ugly</i>, <i>foul</i>, <i>deformed.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: nasus, Cat. 
			 41, 3: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">res,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 7, § 97</span></i>
			 Müll.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jocus in (rebus) turpiculis et quasi deformibus
					ponitur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 2, 61, 248</span></i>
			.</div>
